{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"synthetic media synthetic media","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md","fileName":"Synthetic Media.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Synthetic Media","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Ethics and Digital Power]], [[Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","aiethics.epub","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"synthetic media synthetic media","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md","fileName":"Synthetic Media.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Synthetic Media","heading":"Synthetic Media","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Synthetic media are images, audio, video, or text generated or altered so that fabricated content can appear authentic. AI lowers the effort required to imitate people, invent events, and automate persuasive communication.\n\nThe ethical harm includes more than a single deception. When fabricated media become common, genuine evidence can also be dismissed as fake, weakening trust in communication and public institutions. Bots can amplify the effect by simulating social agreement or overwhelming discussion. Disclosure of artificial identity and methods for verification help, but the broader problem concerns the social conditions under which people decide what to believe.\n\nFrom a forensic perspective, computer-generated faces and scenes may omit traces of physical image formation, including camera-sensor correlations or subtle physiological signals. Machine-learning systems can rapidly improve after a detector becomes known, so these artifacts are evidence about a particular generation pipeline rather than permanent proof that all synthetic media will share the same flaw.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","aiethics.epub","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"synthetic media synthetic media","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Synthetic Media.md","fileName":"Synthetic Media.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Synthetic Media","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]\n\n[[fakephotos.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","aiethics.epub","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}